{
  "_authority": { "schemaVersion": 1, "defaultDisposition": "settled", "numericValues": "playtestTuning", "playerFacingCopy": "provisionalCopy" },
  "_note": "PLACEHOLDER costs. ALL research lives here, gated behind themed branches with prerequisites — there is no flat shopping list anywhere in the game. A node is a one-time unlock; repeatable things (shelving I/II/III) are separate nodes chained by 'requires', which keeps the tree honest and removes the idea of ranks entirely. 'grants' is what unlocking it hands you: a gambit component, a symbol, or an effect on base state. The Hold's ladder runs long and gets steeply expensive on purpose (decisions-session-16 §2): three tiers capped storage at twenty slots forever, which fights the hoarding pillar. With materials binning by kind the ladder is buying room for *variety* rather than for volume. PLACEHOLDER costs. PENMANSHIP LIVES AT THE SCRIPTORIUM and has NO free rungs (Aimee, 6 Aug: 'the player MUST meet the calligrapher to progress. it's core to the game'). That is a stated exception to Q40's rule that a building's first rungs stay reachable — the rule protects capacity, and the hands are not a convenience, they are what the game is about. The hands were also badly underpriced: a pencil roughly doubles what a page can say and cost less than a storehouse tier. Each hand now names a rare material from a specific kind of world, so upgrading your hand means going and writing for it. 'lead' from the spec is copper here — the ductile metal that already exists. 'needsStationTier' gates a node on its building's tier, which is the job maxTier never had. 7 Aug: the four generic 'instruments' nodes at the Workshop were a placeholder for clause-audit F2 — each +1 analysis tier, bought from a menu. crafting-spec.md PART TWO specs the real thing and it is better: EIGHT FIELD INSTRUMENTS at Mara's Survey Post, one per subject, and FOUR PAGE LENS tiers at Isolde's Scriptorium gated on how many instruments you own. Field readings are the currency prediction is bought with, so the lens grows subject by subject as the kit does. Quartz is in six of eight instruments — it is the lens material, which is the job sigil-vocabulary.md gave it. Mercury and adamant gate the late ones, which is right: reading time should be the hardest thing to learn. ALL COSTS PLACEHOLDER.",
